window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b285-befa5243e64a0a19.json"]={sha256:"befa5243e64a0a19d46d190394ff50c29af89a187b83e4054531a4734fc67d8f",value:{"id":"b285","title":"海岸養灘工程","titleEn":"Beach nourishment","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以泥沙守恆與監測辨識養灘的短期重塑和長期功能。課程從邊界辨識與資料整理走到水理量化、構造介面及驗證紀錄；每一步把計算結果連回可量測的證據。十個不同單元分別處理關鍵機制，不以名義尺寸或單一通過率代替整體工程判斷，並明列合成算例與現地資料的差別。","summaryEn":"Distinguish nourishment reshaping and long-term function through sediment accounting and monitoring. The course moves from boundary identification and evidence to hydraulic quantification, structural interfaces and verification records. Ten distinct units connect each calculated quantity to measurable evidence. Nominal geometry or a single pass rate does not establish whole-system performance, and synthetic teaching examples remain separate from field observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-coast","architectureNodes":[["養灘幾何與方量","Nourishment geometry and volume"],["粒徑相容性","Grain-size compatibility"],["沿岸泥沙收支","Alongshore sediment budget"],["暴風後剖面恢復","Post-storm profile recovery"],["沉降與水平輸運","Settling and horizontal advection"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-coast","labels":["養灘幾何與方量","粒徑相容性","沿岸泥沙收支","暴風後剖面恢復","沉降與水平輸運"],"labelsEn":["Nourishment geometry and volume","Grain-size compatibility","Alongshore sediment budget","Post-storm profile recovery","Settling and horizontal advection"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創合成算例，不是地標工程的實測或推薦操作值。教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設長1000m、增寬20m、等厚1.5m，V=Lbt=30000m³；只作矩形填方示意，不是平衡剖面設計。假設增寬由20改為22m而長度、厚度不變，方量30000增至33000m³，增加10%；並不代表養灘維持時間增加10%。重新計算前先列固定條件、單位、適用尺度及可能失效的邊界。把模型敏感度與測量誤差分開，不能將單一參數變化直接當成工程風險或壽命比例。比較兩次結果後，記錄還需要哪些獨立證據，並由負責專業人員判斷適用性。","textEn":"This original synthetic example is neither a landmark measurement nor a recommended operating value. Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume length1000m, added width20m and uniform thickness1.5m. V=Lbt=30000m³ is rectangular accounting, not equilibrium-profile design. Increasing added width from20 to22m at fixed length and thickness raises volume from30000 to33000m³ by10%, without implying10% longer retention. Before recalculating, list fixed conditions, units, applicable scale and boundaries that could fail. Separate model sensitivity from measurement uncertainty: a parameter change does not directly give a proportional change in engineering risk or service life. Compare the results, record independent evidence still needed, and have the responsible specialist determine applicability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b285-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「養灘幾何與方量」與「固體量與孔隙」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Nourishment geometry and volume\" and \"Solid quantity and porosity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b285-v15-01","title":"養灘幾何與方量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Nourishment geometry and volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「養灘幾何與方量」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Nourishment geometry and volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"養灘計量先界定施工面、斷面及高程基準，填入的鬆方與完成後剖面方量不必相等。矩形示意適合練習尺寸核對，真實海灘有斜坡與沿岸變化，需要逐剖面積分；初始灘寬也不保證風浪重塑後仍維持相同位置。 假設長1000m、增寬20m、等厚1.5m，V=Lbt=30000m³；只作矩形填方示意，不是平衡剖面設計。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「養灘幾何與方量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Nourishment accounting begins with placement limits, sections and a vertical datum. Delivered loose volume need not equal completed profile volume. A rectangular illustration helps check dimensions, but a real beach varies alongshore and across its slopes and requires section integration; initial width does not guarantee the same shoreline after wave-driven redistribution. Assume length1000m, added width20m and uniform thickness1.5m. V=Lbt=30000m³ is rectangular accounting, not equilibrium-profile design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Nourishment geometry and volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「養灘幾何與方量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Nourishment geometry and volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-01-k1","title":"養灘幾何與方量","titleEn":"Nourishment geometry and volume","text":"養灘計量先界定施工面、斷面及高程基準，填入的鬆方與完成後剖面方量不必相等。矩形示意適合練習尺寸核對，真實海灘有斜坡與沿岸變化，需要逐剖面積分；初始灘寬也不保證風浪重塑後仍維持相同位置。","textEn":"Nourishment accounting begins with placement limits, sections and a vertical datum. Delivered loose volume need not equal completed profile volume.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「養灘幾何與方量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Nourishment geometry and volume\" is correct?","options":["施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。","養灘計量先界定施工面、斷面及高程基準，填入的鬆方與完成後剖面方量不必相等。","孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。"],"optionsEn":["The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season.","Nourishment accounting begins with placement limits, sections and a vertical datum.","Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains."],"answer":1,"explanation":"養灘計量先界定施工面、斷面及高程基準，填入的鬆方與完成後剖面方量不必相等。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Nourishment accounting begins with placement limits, sections and a vertical datum. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b285-v15-02","title":"養灘幾何與方量：定量估算","titleEn":"Nourishment geometry and volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「養灘幾何與方量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Nourishment geometry and volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設長1000m、增寬20m、等厚1.5m，V=Lbt=30000m³；只作矩形填方示意，不是平衡剖面設計。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume length1000m, added width20m and uniform thickness1.5m. V=Lbt=30000m³ is rectangular accounting, not equilibrium-profile design. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設長1000m、增寬20m、等厚1.5m，V=Lbt=30000m³；只作矩形填方示意，不是平衡剖面設計。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume length1000m, added width20m and uniform thickness1.5m. V=Lbt=30000m³ is rectangular accounting, not equilibrium-profile design.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「養灘幾何與方量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Nourishment geometry and volume\", which statement holds?","options":["新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。","乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement.","Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b285-v15-03","title":"養灘幾何與方量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Nourishment geometry and volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「養灘幾何與方量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Nourishment geometry and volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。核對計量採原狀、鬆方或完成方，與運輸票據比較差異時保留孔隙和含水定義。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area. State whether quantities are in-situ, loose or completed volumes; retain porosity and moisture definitions when comparing survey totals with delivery records. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。核對計量採原狀、鬆方或完成方，與運輸票據比較差異時保留孔隙和含水定義。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area. State whether quantities are in-situ, loose or completed volumes; retain porosity and moisture definitions when comparing survey totals with delivery records.","failure":"注意干擾：用車船鬆方直接代替完成灘體會把孔隙變化誤認為流失，缺少近岸水下剖面又會漏掉重分布砂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Substituting delivered loose volume for completed beach volume confuses porosity change with loss. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。核對計量採原狀、鬆方或完成方，與運輸票據比較差異時保留孔隙和含水定義。","textEn":"Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area. State whether quantities are in-situ, loose or completed volumes; retain porosity and moisture definitions when comparing survey totals with delivery records.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。核對計量採原狀、鬆方或完成方，與運輸票據比較差異時保留孔隙和含水定義。","textEn":"Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area. State whether quantities are in-situ, loose or completed volumes; retain porosity and moisture definitions when comparing survey totals with delivery records.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「養灘幾何與方量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Nourishment geometry and volume\"?","options":["在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。"],"optionsEn":["Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b285-v15-04","title":"養灘幾何與方量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Nourishment geometry and volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「養灘幾何與方量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Nourishment geometry and volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用車船鬆方直接代替完成灘體會把孔隙變化誤認為流失，缺少近岸水下剖面又會漏掉重分布砂。表面變寬不能單獨證明整個活動剖面已增加足夠儲砂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Substituting delivered loose volume for completed beach volume confuses porosity change with loss. Missing submerged sections conceal redistributed sand, and a wider dry beach alone does not establish added storage across the active profile. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設長1000m、增寬20m、等厚1.5m，V=Lbt=30000m³；只作矩形填方示意，不是平衡剖面設計。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: V=Lbt=30000m³ is rectangular accounting, not equilibrium-profile design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用車船鬆方直接代替完成灘體會把孔隙變化誤認為流失，缺少近岸水下剖面又會漏掉重分布砂。表面變寬不能單獨證明整個活動剖面已增加足夠儲砂。","textEn":"Substituting delivered loose volume for completed beach volume confuses porosity change with loss. Missing submerged sections conceal redistributed sand, and a wider dry beach alone does not establish added storage across the active profile.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「養灘幾何與方量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Nourishment geometry and volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","用車船鬆方直接代替完成灘體會把孔隙變化誤認為流失，缺少近岸水下剖面又會漏掉重分布砂。","孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Substituting delivered loose volume for completed beach volume confuses porosity change with loss.","Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用車船鬆方直接代替完成灘體會把孔隙變化誤認為流失，缺少近岸水下剖面又會漏掉重分布砂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Substituting delivered loose volume for completed beach volume confuses porosity change with loss. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b285-v15-05","title":"固體量與孔隙：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Solid quantity and porosity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「固體量與孔隙」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Solid quantity and porosity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"養灘材料以固體顆粒量追蹤比較穩定，因為排水及壓密會改變外觀體積。乾質量換算需用顆粒密度而非濕容重，孔隙率亦須對應相同材料狀態；黏土團塊或貝殼會使單一密度近似失準，不能只憑船艙刻度結算泥沙收支。 假設鬆方10000m³、孔隙率0.40、顆粒密度2650kg/m³，乾砂質量V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg；不含孔隙水。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「固體量與孔隙」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Tracking solid grains helps distinguish material movement from drainage and compaction. Dry-mass conversion requires grain density rather than wet bulk density, with porosity defined for the same condition. Clay aggregates or shells can invalidate a single-density approximation, so hopper readings alone cannot close the sediment balance. Assume bulk volume10000m³, porosity0.40 and grain density2650kg/m³. Dry mass V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg, excluding pore water. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Solid quantity and porosity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「固體量與孔隙」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Solid quantity and porosity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-05-k1","title":"固體量與孔隙","titleEn":"Solid quantity and porosity","text":"養灘材料以固體顆粒量追蹤比較穩定，因為排水及壓密會改變外觀體積。乾質量換算需用顆粒密度而非濕容重，孔隙率亦須對應相同材料狀態；黏土團塊或貝殼會使單一密度近似失準，不能只憑船艙刻度結算泥沙收支。","textEn":"Tracking solid grains helps distinguish material movement from drainage and compaction. Dry-mass conversion requires grain density rather than wet bulk density, with porosity defined for the same condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「固體量與孔隙」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Solid quantity and porosity\" is correct?","options":["孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。","借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。","養灘材料以固體顆粒量追蹤比較穩定，因為排水及壓密會改變外觀體積。"],"optionsEn":["Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains.","A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.","Tracking solid grains helps distinguish material movement from drainage and compaction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"養灘材料以固體顆粒量追蹤比較穩定，因為排水及壓密會改變外觀體積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Tracking solid grains helps distinguish material movement from drainage and compaction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b285-v15-06","title":"固體量與孔隙：定量估算","titleEn":"Solid quantity and porosity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「固體量與孔隙」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Solid quantity and porosity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設鬆方10000m³、孔隙率0.40、顆粒密度2650kg/m³，乾砂質量V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg；不含孔隙水。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume bulk volume10000m³, porosity0.40 and grain density2650kg/m³. Dry mass V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg, excluding pore water. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設鬆方10000m³、孔隙率0.40、顆粒密度2650kg/m³，乾砂質量V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg；不含孔隙水。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume bulk volume10000m³, porosity0.40 and grain density2650kg/m³. Dry mass V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg, excluding pore water.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「固體量與孔隙」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Solid quantity and porosity\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。","暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month.","All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b285-v15-07","title":"固體量與孔隙：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Solid quantity and porosity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「固體量與孔隙」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Solid quantity and porosity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。把含水造成的重量變化和真正乾固體輸入分開，再檢查換算是否使用同一孔隙定義。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates. Separate water-weight changes from dry-solid input, and verify that every conversion uses the same definition of void space. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。把含水造成的重量變化和真正乾固體輸入分開，再檢查換算是否使用同一孔隙定義。","observationEn":"Site practice: Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates. Separate water-weight changes from dry-solid input, and verify that every conversion uses the same definition of void space.","failure":"注意干擾：若濕砂質量被當成乾砂，輸入固體會被高估，排水後看似大量砂消失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating wet mass as dry mass overstates solid input and makes drainage resemble major sand loss. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。把含水造成的重量變化和真正乾固體輸入分開，再檢查換算是否使用同一孔隙定義。","textEn":"Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates. Separate water-weight changes from dry-solid input, and verify that every conversion uses the same definition of void space.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。把含水造成的重量變化和真正乾固體輸入分開，再檢查換算是否使用同一孔隙定義。","textEn":"Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates. Separate water-weight changes from dry-solid input, and verify that every conversion uses the same definition of void space.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「固體量與孔隙」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Solid quantity and porosity\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。","濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates.","An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b285-v15-08","title":"固體量與孔隙：失效診斷","titleEn":"Solid quantity and porosity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「固體量與孔隙」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Solid quantity and porosity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若濕砂質量被當成乾砂，輸入固體會被高估，排水後看似大量砂消失。不同批次含貝殼與細料時，沿用同一密度也可能製造不存在的收支缺口。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating wet mass as dry mass overstates solid input and makes drainage resemble major sand loss. Variable shell and fine content also makes a single borrowed density create an artificial deficit in the sediment budget. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設鬆方10000m³、孔隙率0.40、顆粒密度2650kg/m³，乾砂質量V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg；不含孔隙水。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Dry mass V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg, excluding pore water.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若濕砂質量被當成乾砂，輸入固體會被高估，排水後看似大量砂消失。不同批次含貝殼與細料時，沿用同一密度也可能製造不存在的收支缺口。","textEn":"Treating wet mass as dry mass overstates solid input and makes drainage resemble major sand loss. Variable shell and fine content also makes a single borrowed density create an artificial deficit in the sediment budget.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「固體量與孔隙」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Solid quantity and porosity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。","若濕砂質量被當成乾砂，輸入固體會被高估，排水後看似大量砂消失。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.","Treating wet mass as dry mass overstates solid input and makes drainage resemble major sand loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若濕砂質量被當成乾砂，輸入固體會被高估，排水後看似大量砂消失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating wet mass as dry mass overstates solid input and makes drainage resemble major sand loss. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b285-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「粒徑相容性」與「活動剖面平移」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Grain-size compatibility\" and \"Active-profile translation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b285-v15-09","title":"粒徑相容性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Grain-size compatibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「粒徑相容性」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grain-size compatibility” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"借砂與原灘的中值粒徑可作第一層比較，但單一比值會隱藏級配、細料與顆粒形狀。不同粒群在波流中有不同沉降及搬運行為，較粗不必然在所有位置都更好；材料選擇還牽涉生態、灘坡和使用功能，需把各種證據並列。 假設借砂D50=0.45mm、原灘D50=0.30mm，比值1.50；不能據此單獨判定全級配相容或保留率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「粒徑相容性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Median size offers an initial comparison between borrow material and native sand, but one ratio hides grading, fines and particle shape. Different fractions settle and move differently under waves and currents. Coarser is not universally better, and selection also involves ecology, beach slope and intended use, requiring several complementary observations. Assume borrow D50=0.45mm and native D50=0.30mm. Their ratio is1.50; this alone establishes neither grading compatibility nor retention. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grain-size compatibility” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「粒徑相容性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grain-size compatibility”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-09-k1","title":"粒徑相容性","titleEn":"Grain-size compatibility","text":"借砂與原灘的中值粒徑可作第一層比較，但單一比值會隱藏級配、細料與顆粒形狀。不同粒群在波流中有不同沉降及搬運行為，較粗不必然在所有位置都更好；材料選擇還牽涉生態、灘坡和使用功能，需把各種證據並列。","textEn":"Median size offers an initial comparison between borrow material and native sand, but one ratio hides grading, fines and particle shape. Different fractions settle and move differently under waves and currents.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「粒徑相容性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Grain-size compatibility\" is correct?","options":["借砂與原灘的中值粒徑可作第一層比較，但單一比值會隱藏級配、細料與顆粒形狀。","借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。","新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。"],"optionsEn":["Median size offers an initial comparison between borrow material and native sand, but one ratio hides grading, fines and particle shape.","A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.","Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"借砂與原灘的中值粒徑可作第一層比較，但單一比值會隱藏級配、細料與顆粒形狀。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Median size offers an initial comparison between borrow material and native sand, but one ratio hides grading, fines and particle shape. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b285-v15-10","title":"粒徑相容性：定量估算","titleEn":"Grain-size compatibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「粒徑相容性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grain-size compatibility” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設借砂D50=0.45mm、原灘D50=0.30mm，比值1.50；不能據此單獨判定全級配相容或保留率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume borrow D50=0.45mm and native D50=0.30mm. Their ratio is1.50; this alone establishes neither grading compatibility nor retention. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設借砂D50=0.45mm、原灘D50=0.30mm，比值1.50；不能據此單獨判定全級配相容或保留率。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume borrow D50=0.45mm and native D50=0.30mm. Their ratio is1.50; this alone establishes neither grading compatibility nor retention.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「粒徑相容性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Grain-size compatibility\", which statement holds?","options":["乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。"],"optionsEn":["Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b285-v15-11","title":"粒徑相容性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Grain-size compatibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「粒徑相容性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grain-size compatibility” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。另記顆粒形狀、污染篩查與原灘季節變化，說明哪些物理或環境條件仍沒有代表性樣本。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians. Record particle shape, contaminant screening and seasonal native variability, identifying physical or environmental conditions for which representative field samples remain unavailable. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。另記顆粒形狀、污染篩查與原灘季節變化，說明哪些物理或環境條件仍沒有代表性樣本。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians. Record particle shape, contaminant screening and seasonal native variability, identifying physical or environmental conditions for which representative field samples remain unavailable.","failure":"注意干擾：中值相同的兩批材料可能有完全不同的細料尾端，入水後一批產生長距離濁羽、另一批迅速沉降。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Two materials with identical medians may have very different fine tails; one generates a long plume while another settles quickly. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。另記顆粒形狀、污染篩查與原灘季節變化，說明哪些物理或環境條件仍沒有代表性樣本。","textEn":"Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians. Record particle shape, contaminant screening and seasonal native variability, identifying physical or environmental conditions for which representative field samples remain unavailable.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。另記顆粒形狀、污染篩查與原灘季節變化，說明哪些物理或環境條件仍沒有代表性樣本。","textEn":"Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians. Record particle shape, contaminant screening and seasonal native variability, identifying physical or environmental conditions for which representative field samples remain unavailable.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「粒徑相容性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Grain-size compatibility\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。","將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again.","Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b285-v15-12","title":"粒徑相容性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Grain-size compatibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「粒徑相容性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grain-size compatibility” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"中值相同的兩批材料可能有完全不同的細料尾端，入水後一批產生長距離濁羽、另一批迅速沉降。只使用中值配比會錯估輸運與環境影響。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Two materials with identical medians may have very different fine tails; one generates a long plume while another settles quickly. Median-only matching therefore misrepresents both transport behavior and environmental consequences of placement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設借砂D50=0.45mm、原灘D50=0.30mm，比值1.50；不能據此單獨判定全級配相容或保留率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Their ratio is1.50; this alone establishes neither grading compatibility nor retention.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"中值相同的兩批材料可能有完全不同的細料尾端，入水後一批產生長距離濁羽、另一批迅速沉降。只使用中值配比會錯估輸運與環境影響。","textEn":"Two materials with identical medians may have very different fine tails; one generates a long plume while another settles quickly. Median-only matching therefore misrepresents both transport behavior and environmental consequences of placement.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「粒徑相容性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Grain-size compatibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["中值相同的兩批材料可能有完全不同的細料尾端，入水後一批產生長距離濁羽、另一批迅速沉降。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。"],"optionsEn":["Two materials with identical medians may have very different fine tails; one generates a long plume while another settles quickly.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"中值相同的兩批材料可能有完全不同的細料尾端，入水後一批產生長距離濁羽、另一批迅速沉降。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Two materials with identical medians may have very different fine tails; one generates a long plume while another settles quickly. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b285-v15-13","title":"活動剖面平移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Active-profile translation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「活動剖面平移」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Active-profile translation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"把新增體積分配到假想活動剖面，可估計岸線平移的量級，但須先指定陸側高度與閉合水深。實際剖面會調整坡度並沿岸交換泥沙，閉合深度也受觀測期影響；平行平移只是一項幾何假設，不能將計算結果直接當成施工後岸線預測。 假設V=30000m³、沿岸長1000m、閉合深5m、陸側高2m，Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m；只限平行平移。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「活動剖面平移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Distributing added volume across an assumed active profile gives a shoreline-displacement scale after specifying berm elevation and closure depth. Real profiles change slope and exchange sand alongshore, and closure depth depends on the observation period. Parallel translation is a geometric assumption, not a direct forecast of the actual post-construction beach shoreline. Assume V=30000m³, length1000m, closure depth5m and berm elevation2m. Parallel translation Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Active-profile translation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「活動剖面平移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Active-profile translation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-13-k1","title":"活動剖面平移","titleEn":"Active-profile translation","text":"把新增體積分配到假想活動剖面，可估計岸線平移的量級，但須先指定陸側高度與閉合水深。實際剖面會調整坡度並沿岸交換泥沙，閉合深度也受觀測期影響；平行平移只是一項幾何假設，不能將計算結果直接當成施工後岸線預測。","textEn":"Distributing added volume across an assumed active profile gives a shoreline-displacement scale after specifying berm elevation and closure depth. Real profiles change slope and exchange sand alongshore, and closure depth depends on the observation period.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「活動剖面平移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Active-profile translation\" is correct?","options":["新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。","把新增體積分配到假想活動剖面，可估計岸線平移的量級，但須先指定陸側高度與閉合水深。","年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。"],"optionsEn":["Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement.","Distributing added volume across an assumed active profile gives a shoreline-displacement scale after specifying berm elevation and closure depth.","An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把新增體積分配到假想活動剖面，可估計岸線平移的量級，但須先指定陸側高度與閉合水深。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Distributing added volume across an assumed active profile gives a shoreline-displacement scale after specifying berm elevation and closure depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b285-v15-14","title":"活動剖面平移：定量估算","titleEn":"Active-profile translation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「活動剖面平移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Active-profile translation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設V=30000m³、沿岸長1000m、閉合深5m、陸側高2m，Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m；只限平行平移。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume V=30000m³, length1000m, closure depth5m and berm elevation2m. Parallel translation Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設V=30000m³、沿岸長1000m、閉合深5m、陸側高2m，Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m；只限平行平移。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume V=30000m³, length1000m, closure depth5m and berm elevation2m. Parallel translation Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「活動剖面平移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Active-profile translation\", which statement holds?","options":["暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。","濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast.","An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b285-v15-15","title":"活動剖面平移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Active-profile translation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「活動剖面平移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Active-profile translation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。用多季節水陸聯測剖面比較實際重塑，將沿岸漏失、坡形變化及測量誤差另列，不強迫資料吻合平移。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths. Compare multiple seasonal land-and-water surveys with the translation estimate, listing alongshore exchange, slope adjustment and measurement error rather than forcing the measured observations to fit. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。用多季節水陸聯測剖面比較實際重塑，將沿岸漏失、坡形變化及測量誤差另列，不強迫資料吻合平移。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths. Compare multiple seasonal land-and-water surveys with the translation estimate, listing alongshore exchange, slope adjustment and measurement error rather than forcing the measured observations to fit.","failure":"注意干擾：把短期觀測不到變化的位置當成永久閉合深度，會高估岸線移動量；若近岸形成砂壩，材料仍在剖面內卻未出現在乾灘，使僅看岸線的判讀失真。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating a temporarily inactive depth as permanent closure can overstate shoreline movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。用多季節水陸聯測剖面比較實際重塑，將沿岸漏失、坡形變化及測量誤差另列，不強迫資料吻合平移。","textEn":"Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths. Compare multiple seasonal land-and-water surveys with the translation estimate, listing alongshore exchange, slope adjustment and measurement error rather than forcing the measured observations to fit.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。用多季節水陸聯測剖面比較實際重塑，將沿岸漏失、坡形變化及測量誤差另列，不強迫資料吻合平移。","textEn":"Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths. Compare multiple seasonal land-and-water surveys with the translation estimate, listing alongshore exchange, slope adjustment and measurement error rather than forcing the measured observations to fit.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「活動剖面平移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Active-profile translation\"?","options":["清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。"],"optionsEn":["Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season."],"answer":0,"explanation":"清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b285-v15-16","title":"活動剖面平移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Active-profile translation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「活動剖面平移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Active-profile translation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把短期觀測不到變化的位置當成永久閉合深度，會高估岸線移動量；若近岸形成砂壩，材料仍在剖面內卻未出現在乾灘，使僅看岸線的判讀失真。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating a temporarily inactive depth as permanent closure can overstate shoreline movement. A nearshore bar may retain sand within the profile without widening the dry beach, misleading interpretations based on shoreline position alone. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設V=30000m³、沿岸長1000m、閉合深5m、陸側高2m，Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m；只限平行平移。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Parallel translation Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把短期觀測不到變化的位置當成永久閉合深度，會高估岸線移動量；若近岸形成砂壩，材料仍在剖面內卻未出現在乾灘，使僅看岸線的判讀失真。","textEn":"Treating a temporarily inactive depth as permanent closure can overstate shoreline movement. A nearshore bar may retain sand within the profile without widening the dry beach, misleading interpretations based on shoreline position alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「活動剖面平移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Active-profile translation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把短期觀測不到變化的位置當成永久閉合深度，會高估岸線移動量；若近岸形成砂壩，材料仍在剖面內卻未出現在乾灘，使僅看岸線的判讀失真。","年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Treating a temporarily inactive depth as permanent closure can overstate shoreline movement.","An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把短期觀測不到變化的位置當成永久閉合深度，會高估岸線移動量；若近岸形成砂壩，材料仍在剖面內卻未出現在乾灘，使僅看岸線的判讀失真。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating a temporarily inactive depth as permanent closure can overstate shoreline movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b285-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「沿岸泥沙收支」與「壓密與體積變化」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Alongshore sediment budget\" and \"Compaction and apparent volume loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b285-v15-17","title":"沿岸泥沙收支：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Alongshore sediment budget: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「沿岸泥沙收支」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alongshore sediment budget” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"養灘區不是封閉容器，上下游輸砂差和跨岸交換共同改變儲砂。年度平均通量只適合所定義邊界與時段，暴風、港口阻砂及補砂事件可能打破平穩假設；應先確認輸入輸出各自的符號與單位，再討論需要維持的功能。 假設僅沿岸輸入30000、輸出45000m³/year，dV/dt=−15000m³/year；若通量固定5year，儲量減75000m³。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沿岸泥沙收支」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A nourishment reach is not a sealed container: alongshore flux differences and cross-shore exchange alter storage. Annual mean transport applies only to its specified boundaries and period. Storms, harbor interception and new placements can break stationarity, so signs and units must be established before discussing the intended coastal function to maintain. Assume only alongshore input30000 and output45000m³/year. dV/dt=−15000m³/year; fixed fluxes over5years reduce storage75000m³. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alongshore sediment budget” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沿岸泥沙收支」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alongshore sediment budget”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-17-k1","title":"沿岸泥沙收支","titleEn":"Alongshore sediment budget","text":"養灘區不是封閉容器，上下游輸砂差和跨岸交換共同改變儲砂。年度平均通量只適合所定義邊界與時段，暴風、港口阻砂及補砂事件可能打破平穩假設；應先確認輸入輸出各自的符號與單位，再討論需要維持的功能。","textEn":"A nourishment reach is not a sealed container: alongshore flux differences and cross-shore exchange alter storage. Annual mean transport applies only to its specified boundaries and period.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沿岸泥沙收支」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Alongshore sediment budget\" is correct?","options":["年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。","乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。","養灘區不是封閉容器，上下游輸砂差和跨岸交換共同改變儲砂。"],"optionsEn":["An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month.","Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.","A nourishment reach is not a sealed container: alongshore flux differences and cross-shore exchange alter storage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"養灘區不是封閉容器，上下游輸砂差和跨岸交換共同改變儲砂。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A nourishment reach is not a sealed container: alongshore flux differences and cross-shore exchange alter storage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b285-v15-18","title":"沿岸泥沙收支：定量估算","titleEn":"Alongshore sediment budget: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沿岸泥沙收支」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alongshore sediment budget” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設僅沿岸輸入30000、輸出45000m³/year，dV/dt=−15000m³/year；若通量固定5year，儲量減75000m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume only alongshore input30000 and output45000m³/year. dV/dt=−15000m³/year; fixed fluxes over5years reduce storage75000m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設僅沿岸輸入30000、輸出45000m³/year，dV/dt=−15000m³/year；若通量固定5year，儲量減75000m³。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume only alongshore input30000 and output45000m³/year. dV/dt=−15000m³/year; fixed fluxes over5years reduce storage75000m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沿岸泥沙收支」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Alongshore sediment budget\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。","粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero.","Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b285-v15-19","title":"沿岸泥沙收支：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Alongshore sediment budget: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沿岸泥沙收支」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alongshore sediment budget” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。用獨立地形差量測試收支殘差，並把不同年份的風暴條件分開而不是只看長期平均。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways. Test budget residuals against independent elevation change and distinguish storm conditions between years rather than relying exclusively on a single long-term average. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。用獨立地形差量測試收支殘差，並把不同年份的風暴條件分開而不是只看長期平均。","observationEn":"Site practice: Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways. Test budget residuals against independent elevation change and distinguish storm conditions between years rather than relying exclusively on a single long-term average.","failure":"注意干擾：同一砂量在兩個相鄰邊界重複計入會製造假盈餘，忽略跨岸砂壩交換則容易將季節儲存誤認永久流失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Double-counting sediment at adjacent boundaries creates an artificial surplus, while omitted cross-shore bar exchange makes seasonal storage resemble permanent loss. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。用獨立地形差量測試收支殘差，並把不同年份的風暴條件分開而不是只看長期平均。","textEn":"Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways. Test budget residuals against independent elevation change and distinguish storm conditions between years rather than relying exclusively on a single long-term average.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。用獨立地形差量測試收支殘差，並把不同年份的風暴條件分開而不是只看長期平均。","textEn":"Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways. Test budget residuals against independent elevation change and distinguish storm conditions between years rather than relying exclusively on a single long-term average.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沿岸泥沙收支」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Alongshore sediment budget\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。","孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways.","Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b285-v15-20","title":"沿岸泥沙收支：失效診斷","titleEn":"Alongshore sediment budget: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沿岸泥沙收支」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alongshore sediment budget” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同一砂量在兩個相鄰邊界重複計入會製造假盈餘，忽略跨岸砂壩交換則容易將季節儲存誤認永久流失。平穩外推也可能低估一次大事件的主導作用。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Double-counting sediment at adjacent boundaries creates an artificial surplus, while omitted cross-shore bar exchange makes seasonal storage resemble permanent loss. Stationary extrapolation can also miss the dominant influence of one large event. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設僅沿岸輸入30000、輸出45000m³/year，dV/dt=−15000m³/year；若通量固定5year，儲量減75000m³。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume only alongshore input30000 and output45000m³/year. dV/dt=−15000m³/year; fixed fluxes over5years reduce storage75000m³.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同一砂量在兩個相鄰邊界重複計入會製造假盈餘，忽略跨岸砂壩交換則容易將季節儲存誤認永久流失。平穩外推也可能低估一次大事件的主導作用。","textEn":"Double-counting sediment at adjacent boundaries creates an artificial surplus, while omitted cross-shore bar exchange makes seasonal storage resemble permanent loss. Stationary extrapolation can also miss the dominant influence of one large event.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沿岸泥沙收支」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Alongshore sediment budget\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。","同一砂量在兩個相鄰邊界重複計入會製造假盈餘，忽略跨岸砂壩交換則容易將季節儲存誤認永久流失。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.","Double-counting sediment at adjacent boundaries creates an artificial surplus, while omitted cross-shore bar exchange makes seasonal storage resemble permanent loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同一砂量在兩個相鄰邊界重複計入會製造假盈餘，忽略跨岸砂壩交換則容易將季節儲存誤認永久流失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Double-counting sediment at adjacent boundaries creates an artificial surplus, while omitted cross-shore bar exchange makes seasonal storage resemble permanent loss. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b285-v15-21","title":"壓密與體積變化：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Compaction and apparent volume loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「壓密與體積變化」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Compaction and apparent volume loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"同一乾固體量隨孔隙改變而呈現不同鬆方，養灘完工後地形下降不一定全是輸砂。需要把粒子輸出和孔隙水排除分開，同時注意級配分選會改變密實狀態；幾何測量提供外形，而固體收支才幫助辨認真正材料流失。 假設固體體積18000m³保持不變，孔隙率0.40時鬆方30000m³，降到0.35後V=18000/0.65=27692.3m³。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓密與體積變化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An unchanged quantity of solids occupies different bulk volumes as porosity changes, so post-placement lowering need not be entirely sediment transport. Separate particle export from drainage while recognizing that sorting changes packing. Geometry describes the exterior, whereas solid accounting helps identify actual offshore material loss. Assume unchanged solid volume18000m³. Bulk volume is30000m³ at porosity0.40 and27692.3m³ at porosity0.35, using V=Vs/(1−n). Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Compaction and apparent volume loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壓密與體積變化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Compaction and apparent volume loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-21-k1","title":"壓密與體積變化","titleEn":"Compaction and apparent volume loss","text":"同一乾固體量隨孔隙改變而呈現不同鬆方，養灘完工後地形下降不一定全是輸砂。需要把粒子輸出和孔隙水排除分開，同時注意級配分選會改變密實狀態；幾何測量提供外形，而固體收支才幫助辨認真正材料流失。","textEn":"An unchanged quantity of solids occupies different bulk volumes as porosity changes, so post-placement lowering need not be entirely sediment transport. Separate particle export from drainage while recognizing that sorting changes packing.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓密與體積變化」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Compaction and apparent volume loss\" is correct?","options":["同一乾固體量隨孔隙改變而呈現不同鬆方，養灘完工後地形下降不一定全是輸砂。","乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。","暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。"],"optionsEn":["An unchanged quantity of solids occupies different bulk volumes as porosity changes, so post-placement lowering need not be entirely sediment transport.","Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.","All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同一乾固體量隨孔隙改變而呈現不同鬆方，養灘完工後地形下降不一定全是輸砂。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An unchanged quantity of solids occupies different bulk volumes as porosity changes, so post-placement lowering need not be entirely sediment transport. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b285-v15-22","title":"壓密與體積變化：定量估算","titleEn":"Compaction and apparent volume loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壓密與體積變化」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Compaction and apparent volume loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設固體體積18000m³保持不變，孔隙率0.40時鬆方30000m³，降到0.35後V=18000/0.65=27692.3m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume unchanged solid volume18000m³. Bulk volume is30000m³ at porosity0.40 and27692.3m³ at porosity0.35, using V=Vs/(1−n). Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設固體體積18000m³保持不變，孔隙率0.40時鬆方30000m³，降到0.35後V=18000/0.65=27692.3m³。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume unchanged solid volume18000m³. Bulk volume is30000m³ at porosity0.40 and27692.3m³ at porosity0.35, using V=Vs/(1−n).","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壓密與體積變化」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Compaction and apparent volume loss\", which statement holds?","options":["濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。"],"optionsEn":["An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b285-v15-23","title":"壓密與體積變化：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Compaction and apparent volume loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壓密與體積變化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Compaction and apparent volume loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。保持乾固體定義一致，另查波流輸出證據，避免以任意壓密係數吸收所有量測差異。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space. Maintain a consistent dry-solid definition and inspect transport evidence separately rather than automatically absorbing every discrepancy into an arbitrary compaction factor. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。保持乾固體定義一致，另查波流輸出證據，避免以任意壓密係數吸收所有量測差異。","observationEn":"Site practice: Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space. Maintain a consistent dry-solid definition and inspect transport evidence separately rather than automatically absorbing every discrepancy into an arbitrary compaction factor.","failure":"注意干擾：濕砂表面下降若全部記成侵蝕，會高估維護需求；反過來把真正沖失都稱為壓密，則隱藏砂源不足。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Calling all surface lowering erosion overstates maintenance needs, while labeling real export as compaction conceals inadequate supply. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。保持乾固體定義一致，另查波流輸出證據，避免以任意壓密係數吸收所有量測差異。","textEn":"Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space. Maintain a consistent dry-solid definition and inspect transport evidence separately rather than automatically absorbing every discrepancy into an arbitrary compaction factor.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。保持乾固體定義一致，另查波流輸出證據，避免以任意壓密係數吸收所有量測差異。","textEn":"Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space. Maintain a consistent dry-solid definition and inspect transport evidence separately rather than automatically absorbing every discrepancy into an arbitrary compaction factor.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壓密與體積變化」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Compaction and apparent volume loss\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。","在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.","Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b285-v15-24","title":"壓密與體積變化：失效診斷","titleEn":"Compaction and apparent volume loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壓密與體積變化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Compaction and apparent volume loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"濕砂表面下降若全部記成侵蝕，會高估維護需求；反過來把真正沖失都稱為壓密，則隱藏砂源不足。缺少密度與地形的共同證據無法區分兩種機制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Calling all surface lowering erosion overstates maintenance needs, while labeling real export as compaction conceals inadequate supply. Without paired density and terrain evidence, the two mechanisms cannot reliably be distinguished in the completed beach. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設固體體積18000m³保持不變，孔隙率0.40時鬆方30000m³，降到0.35後V=18000/0.65=27692.3m³。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Bulk volume is30000m³ at porosity0.40 and27692.3m³ at porosity0.35, using V=Vs/(1−n).","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"濕砂表面下降若全部記成侵蝕，會高估維護需求；反過來把真正沖失都稱為壓密，則隱藏砂源不足。缺少密度與地形的共同證據無法區分兩種機制。","textEn":"Calling all surface lowering erosion overstates maintenance needs, while labeling real export as compaction conceals inadequate supply. Without paired density and terrain evidence, the two mechanisms cannot reliably be distinguished in the completed beach.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壓密與體積變化」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Compaction and apparent volume loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["濕砂表面下降若全部記成侵蝕，會高估維護需求；反過來把真正沖失都稱為壓密，則隱藏砂源不足。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。"],"optionsEn":["Calling all surface lowering erosion overstates maintenance needs, while labeling real export as compaction conceals inadequate supply.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast."],"answer":0,"explanation":"濕砂表面下降若全部記成侵蝕，會高估維護需求；反過來把真正沖失都稱為壓密，則隱藏砂源不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Calling all surface lowering erosion overstates maintenance needs, while labeling real export as compaction conceals inadequate supply. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b285-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「暴風後剖面恢復」與「高程偏差與方量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Post-storm profile recovery\" and \"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b285-v15-25","title":"暴風後剖面恢復：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Post-storm profile recovery: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「暴風後剖面恢復」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Post-storm profile recovery” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"暴風可把上灘砂移到水下，後續較緩波況再將部分材料送回，因此恢復率需明示控制範圍與基準。相同乾灘體積恢復不代表粒群或灘形完全恢復，觀測期間亦會左右比例；應同時追蹤總量、位置與功能而非只追一個百分比。 假設固定調查範圍暴風減少20000m³，之後回增8000m³，仍缺12000m³、恢復率40%；未證明其餘砂永久外移。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「暴風後剖面恢復」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Storms can move upper-beach sand offshore and calmer waves return part of it. A recovery fraction therefore requires explicit survey limits and a reference state. Restored dry-beach volume does not imply identical grading or shape, and the observation interval affects the fraction; track quantity, geographical position and function together. Assume a fixed survey area loses20000m³ in a storm and later gains8000m³. Deficit remains12000m³ and recovery is40%, without proving permanent export. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Post-storm profile recovery” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「暴風後剖面恢復」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Post-storm profile recovery”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-25-k1","title":"暴風後剖面恢復","titleEn":"Post-storm profile recovery","text":"暴風可把上灘砂移到水下，後續較緩波況再將部分材料送回，因此恢復率需明示控制範圍與基準。相同乾灘體積恢復不代表粒群或灘形完全恢復，觀測期間亦會左右比例；應同時追蹤總量、位置與功能而非只追一個百分比。","textEn":"Storms can move upper-beach sand offshore and calmer waves return part of it. A recovery fraction therefore requires explicit survey limits and a reference state.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「暴風後剖面恢復」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Post-storm profile recovery\" is correct?","options":["暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。","暴風可把上灘砂移到水下，後續較緩波況再將部分材料送回，因此恢復率需明示控制範圍與基準。","增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。"],"optionsEn":["All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast.","Storms can move upper-beach sand offshore and calmer waves return part of it.","Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暴風可把上灘砂移到水下，後續較緩波況再將部分材料送回，因此恢復率需明示控制範圍與基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Storms can move upper-beach sand offshore and calmer waves return part of it. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b285-v15-26","title":"暴風後剖面恢復：定量估算","titleEn":"Post-storm profile recovery: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「暴風後剖面恢復」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Post-storm profile recovery” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設固定調查範圍暴風減少20000m³，之後回增8000m³，仍缺12000m³、恢復率40%；未證明其餘砂永久外移。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a fixed survey area loses20000m³ in a storm and later gains8000m³. Deficit remains12000m³ and recovery is40%, without proving permanent export. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設固定調查範圍暴風減少20000m³，之後回增8000m³，仍缺12000m³、恢復率40%；未證明其餘砂永久外移。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a fixed survey area loses20000m³ in a storm and later gains8000m³. Deficit remains12000m³ and recovery is40%, without proving permanent export.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「暴風後剖面恢復」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Post-storm profile recovery\", which statement holds?","options":["粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。","孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again.","Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b285-v15-27","title":"暴風後剖面恢復：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Post-storm profile recovery: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「暴風後剖面恢復」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Post-storm profile recovery” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。核對水位和季節條件，將未觀測水深列為未知，而不把那部分材料自動列為損失。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage. Check water level and season, marking unobserved depths as unknown rather than automatically treating their material as lost from the system. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。核對水位和季節條件，將未觀測水深列為未知，而不把那部分材料自動列為損失。","observationEn":"Site practice: Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage. Check water level and season, marking unobserved depths as unknown rather than automatically treating their material as lost from the system.","failure":"注意干擾：恢復期只量乾灘會忽略仍在近岸的庫存，調查邊界移動又可能創造假恢復。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Dry-beach-only monitoring misses nearshore storage, and moving survey boundaries can create artificial recovery. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。核對水位和季節條件，將未觀測水深列為未知，而不把那部分材料自動列為損失。","textEn":"Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage. Check water level and season, marking unobserved depths as unknown rather than automatically treating their material as lost from the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。核對水位和季節條件，將未觀測水深列為未知，而不把那部分材料自動列為損失。","textEn":"Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage. Check water level and season, marking unobserved depths as unknown rather than automatically treating their material as lost from the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「暴風後剖面恢復」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Post-storm profile recovery\"?","options":["保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。"],"optionsEn":["Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b285-v15-28","title":"暴風後剖面恢復：失效診斷","titleEn":"Post-storm profile recovery: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「暴風後剖面恢復」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Post-storm profile recovery” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"恢復期只量乾灘會忽略仍在近岸的庫存，調查邊界移動又可能創造假恢復。若依單一百分比決定補砂，可能反覆搬入材料而沒有處理真正輸砂路徑。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Dry-beach-only monitoring misses nearshore storage, and moving survey boundaries can create artificial recovery. Basing replenishment on one percentage can repeatedly add material without addressing the actual sediment pathways responsible for observed change. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設固定調查範圍暴風減少20000m³，之後回增8000m³，仍缺12000m³、恢復率40%；未證明其餘砂永久外移。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Deficit remains12000m³ and recovery is40%, without proving permanent export.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"恢復期只量乾灘會忽略仍在近岸的庫存，調查邊界移動又可能創造假恢復。若依單一百分比決定補砂，可能反覆搬入材料而沒有處理真正輸砂路徑。","textEn":"Dry-beach-only monitoring misses nearshore storage, and moving survey boundaries can create artificial recovery. Basing replenishment on one percentage can repeatedly add material without addressing the actual sediment pathways responsible for observed change.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「暴風後剖面恢復」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Post-storm profile recovery\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","恢復期只量乾灘會忽略仍在近岸的庫存，調查邊界移動又可能創造假恢復。","增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Dry-beach-only monitoring misses nearshore storage, and moving survey boundaries can create artificial recovery.","Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero."],"answer":1,"explanation":"恢復期只量乾灘會忽略仍在近岸的庫存，調查邊界移動又可能創造假恢復。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Dry-beach-only monitoring misses nearshore storage, and moving survey boundaries can create artificial recovery. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b285-v15-29","title":"高程偏差與方量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「高程偏差與方量」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Elevation bias and volume uncertainty” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大面積相減對共同高程偏差非常敏感，許多測點並不能消除同一基準造成的系統誤差。兩期獨立的整面偏差可用不確定度傳播估計量級，但不能與逐格獨立噪音混為一談；這項區別決定應改善控制點還是加密量測。 假設面積100000m²，兩期各有獨立整面高程標準不確定度0.03m，σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³；不是逐格獨立誤差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高程偏差與方量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Large-area differencing is sensitive to coherent vertical bias, and many points do not remove an error shared by one datum. Independent whole-survey offsets can be propagated to estimate uncertainty, but they must not be confused with independent cell noise; that distinction determines whether better control or denser sampling is needed. Assume area100000m² and independent coherent survey offsets with standard uncertainty0.03m each. σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³, not independent cell error. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Elevation bias and volume uncertainty” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「高程偏差與方量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Elevation bias and volume uncertainty”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-29-k1","title":"高程偏差與方量","titleEn":"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty","text":"大面積相減對共同高程偏差非常敏感，許多測點並不能消除同一基準造成的系統誤差。兩期獨立的整面偏差可用不確定度傳播估計量級，但不能與逐格獨立噪音混為一談；這項區別決定應改善控制點還是加密量測。","textEn":"Large-area differencing is sensitive to coherent vertical bias, and many points do not remove an error shared by one datum. Independent whole-survey offsets can be propagated to estimate uncertainty, but they must not be confused with independent cell noise; that distinction determines whether better control or denser sampling is needed.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高程偏差與方量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty\" is correct?","options":["增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。","濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。","大面積相減對共同高程偏差非常敏感，許多測點並不能消除同一基準造成的系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero.","An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.","Large-area differencing is sensitive to coherent vertical bias, and many points do not remove an error shared by one datum."],"answer":2,"explanation":"大面積相減對共同高程偏差非常敏感，許多測點並不能消除同一基準造成的系統誤差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Large-area differencing is sensitive to coherent vertical bias, and many points do not remove an error shared by one datum. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b285-v15-30","title":"高程偏差與方量：定量估算","titleEn":"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高程偏差與方量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Elevation bias and volume uncertainty” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設面積100000m²，兩期各有獨立整面高程標準不確定度0.03m，σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³；不是逐格獨立誤差。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume area100000m² and independent coherent survey offsets with standard uncertainty0.03m each. σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³, not independent cell error. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設面積100000m²，兩期各有獨立整面高程標準不確定度0.03m，σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³；不是逐格獨立誤差。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume area100000m² and independent coherent survey offsets with standard uncertainty0.03m each. σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³, not independent cell error.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高程偏差與方量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。","借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season.","A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b285-v15-31","title":"高程偏差與方量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高程偏差與方量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Elevation bias and volume uncertainty” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。重算方量差的不確定度時明列相關性，若兩期共用同一偏差則不可直接套獨立平方和。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components. State correlations when propagating volume uncertainty; shared bias across both epochs does not permit the same independent sum-of-squares calculation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。重算方量差的不確定度時明列相關性，若兩期共用同一偏差則不可直接套獨立平方和。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components. State correlations when propagating volume uncertainty; shared bias across both epochs does not permit the same independent sum-of-squares calculation.","failure":"注意干擾：把整面偏差除以測點數平方根會虛構極高精度，使很小的地形差被誤判為侵蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Dividing coherent bias by the square root of point count invents precision and makes small elevation differences appear significant. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。重算方量差的不確定度時明列相關性，若兩期共用同一偏差則不可直接套獨立平方和。","textEn":"Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components. State correlations when propagating volume uncertainty; shared bias across both epochs does not permit the same independent sum-of-squares calculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。重算方量差的不確定度時明列相關性，若兩期共用同一偏差則不可直接套獨立平方和。","textEn":"Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components. State correlations when propagating volume uncertainty; shared bias across both epochs does not permit the same independent sum-of-squares calculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高程偏差與方量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。","年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components.","An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b285-v15-32","title":"高程偏差與方量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高程偏差與方量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elevation bias and volume uncertainty” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把整面偏差除以測點數平方根會虛構極高精度，使很小的地形差被誤判為侵蝕。共同控制點移動也可能讓兩次調查一起偏移而難以自行察覺。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Dividing coherent bias by the square root of point count invents precision and makes small elevation differences appear significant. Moving common control may also shift both surveys together, escaping detection within the survey network itself. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設面積100000m²，兩期各有獨立整面高程標準不確定度0.03m，σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³；不是逐格獨立誤差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume area100000m² and independent coherent survey offsets with standard uncertainty0.03m each. σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³, not independent cell error.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把整面偏差除以測點數平方根會虛構極高精度，使很小的地形差被誤判為侵蝕。共同控制點移動也可能讓兩次調查一起偏移而難以自行察覺。","textEn":"Dividing coherent bias by the square root of point count invents precision and makes small elevation differences appear significant. Moving common control may also shift both surveys together, escaping detection within the survey network itself.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高程偏差與方量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。","把整面偏差除以測點數平方根會虛構極高精度，使很小的地形差被誤判為侵蝕。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.","Dividing coherent bias by the square root of point count invents precision and makes small elevation differences appear significant."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把整面偏差除以測點數平方根會虛構極高精度，使很小的地形差被誤判為侵蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Dividing coherent bias by the square root of point count invents precision and makes small elevation differences appear significant. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b285-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「背景扣除與濁羽通量」與「沉降與水平輸運」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Background correction and plume flux\" and \"Settling and horizontal advection\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b285-v15-33","title":"背景扣除與濁羽通量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Background correction and plume flux: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「背景扣除與濁羽通量」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Background correction and plume flux” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"濁度光學訊號不直接等於懸浮泥沙質量，需要採樣校正且區分自然背景。橫斷面通量取決於濃度與速度的共同分布，均勻完全混合只是示意；估算增量輸送量不能替代環境許可，粒徑、沉降與暴露時間仍須分別解釋。 假設均勻濃度150mg/L、背景20mg/L，增量130mg/L=0.13kg/m³，流量2m³/s，增量質量通量0.26kg/s。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「背景扣除與濁羽通量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An optical turbidity signal is not directly suspended-sediment mass; sampling calibration and background separation are required. Section flux depends jointly on concentration and velocity, with complete uniform mixing only an illustration. Estimated incremental transport does not establish environmental compliance; grading, settling and exposure duration remain separate questions. Assume uniform concentration150mg/L and background20mg/L. Increment130mg/L=0.13kg/m³; at2m³/s, incremental mass flux is0.26kg/s. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Background correction and plume flux” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「背景扣除與濁羽通量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Background correction and plume flux”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-33-k1","title":"背景扣除與濁羽通量","titleEn":"Background correction and plume flux","text":"濁度光學訊號不直接等於懸浮泥沙質量，需要採樣校正且區分自然背景。橫斷面通量取決於濃度與速度的共同分布，均勻完全混合只是示意；估算增量輸送量不能替代環境許可，粒徑、沉降與暴露時間仍須分別解釋。","textEn":"An optical turbidity signal is not directly suspended-sediment mass; sampling calibration and background separation are required. Section flux depends jointly on concentration and velocity, with complete uniform mixing only an illustration.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「背景扣除與濁羽通量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Background correction and plume flux\" is correct?","options":["濁度光學訊號不直接等於懸浮泥沙質量，需要採樣校正且區分自然背景。","濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。","粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。"],"optionsEn":["An optical turbidity signal is not directly suspended-sediment mass; sampling calibration and background separation are required.","An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.","Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again."],"answer":0,"explanation":"濁度光學訊號不直接等於懸浮泥沙質量，需要採樣校正且區分自然背景。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An optical turbidity signal is not directly suspended-sediment mass; sampling calibration and background separation are required. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b285-v15-34","title":"背景扣除與濁羽通量：定量估算","titleEn":"Background correction and plume flux: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「背景扣除與濁羽通量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Background correction and plume flux” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設均勻濃度150mg/L、背景20mg/L，增量130mg/L=0.13kg/m³，流量2m³/s，增量質量通量0.26kg/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume uniform concentration150mg/L and background20mg/L. Increment130mg/L=0.13kg/m³; at2m³/s, incremental mass flux is0.26kg/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設均勻濃度150mg/L、背景20mg/L，增量130mg/L=0.13kg/m³，流量2m³/s，增量質量通量0.26kg/s。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume uniform concentration150mg/L and background20mg/L. Increment130mg/L=0.13kg/m³; at2m³/s, incremental mass flux is0.26kg/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「背景扣除與濁羽通量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Background correction and plume flux\", which statement holds?","options":["孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。"],"optionsEn":["Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b285-v15-35","title":"背景扣除與濁羽通量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Background correction and plume flux: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「背景扣除與濁羽通量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Background correction and plume flux” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。以分層樣本辨識垂向差異，記錄光學校正式及適用粒群，將許可條件和質量計算分別比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume. Use depth-resolved samples to identify stratification, retain optical calibration and applicable grading, and assess permit conditions separately from mass accounting. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。以分層樣本辨識垂向差異，記錄光學校正式及適用粒群，將許可條件和質量計算分別比對。","observationEn":"Site practice: Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume. Use depth-resolved samples to identify stratification, retain optical calibration and applicable grading, and assess permit conditions separately from mass accounting.","failure":"注意干擾：選到已受影響的背景站會低估作業增量，速度和濃度不同時取樣也可能錯配通量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A contaminated background station understates the operational increment, and nonsynchronous concentration and velocity misstate flux. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。以分層樣本辨識垂向差異，記錄光學校正式及適用粒群，將許可條件和質量計算分別比對。","textEn":"Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume. Use depth-resolved samples to identify stratification, retain optical calibration and applicable grading, and assess permit conditions separately from mass accounting.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。以分層樣本辨識垂向差異，記錄光學校正式及適用粒群，將許可條件和質量計算分別比對。","textEn":"Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume. Use depth-resolved samples to identify stratification, retain optical calibration and applicable grading, and assess permit conditions separately from mass accounting.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「背景扣除與濁羽通量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Background correction and plume flux\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。","同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.","Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b285-v15-36","title":"背景扣除與濁羽通量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Background correction and plume flux: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「背景扣除與濁羽通量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Background correction and plume flux” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"選到已受影響的背景站會低估作業增量，速度和濃度不同時取樣也可能錯配通量。儀器讀值下降可能只是粒徑改變，不一定代表輸送質量減少。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A contaminated background station understates the operational increment, and nonsynchronous concentration and velocity misstate flux. Falling optical readings may reflect changed particle size rather than a reduction in the actual mass being transported. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設均勻濃度150mg/L、背景20mg/L，增量130mg/L=0.13kg/m³，流量2m³/s，增量質量通量0.26kg/s。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Increment130mg/L=0.13kg/m³; at2m³/s, incremental mass flux is0.26kg/s.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"選到已受影響的背景站會低估作業增量，速度和濃度不同時取樣也可能錯配通量。儀器讀值下降可能只是粒徑改變，不一定代表輸送質量減少。","textEn":"A contaminated background station understates the operational increment, and nonsynchronous concentration and velocity misstate flux. Falling optical readings may reflect changed particle size rather than a reduction in the actual mass being transported.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「背景扣除與濁羽通量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Background correction and plume flux\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["選到已受影響的背景站會低估作業增量，速度和濃度不同時取樣也可能錯配通量。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。"],"optionsEn":["A contaminated background station understates the operational increment, and nonsynchronous concentration and velocity misstate flux.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again."],"answer":0,"explanation":"選到已受影響的背景站會低估作業增量，速度和濃度不同時取樣也可能錯配通量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A contaminated background station understates the operational increment, and nonsynchronous concentration and velocity misstate flux. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b285-v15-37","title":"沉降與水平輸運：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Settling and horizontal advection: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「沉降與水平輸運」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Settling and horizontal advection” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"粒子沉降與水流搬運的競爭影響落砂區，但真實濁羽還有紊流、絮凝和再懸浮。固定沉速及水平流速模型能建立時間與距離量級，不能將單一結果當成影響邊界；初始釋放深度和海床起伏也需與模型坐標一致。 假設距床3m、沉速0.02m/s、水平流0.30m/s，t=h/ws=150s，x=Ut=45m；忽略紊流與再懸浮。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉降與水平輸運」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Competition between settling and advection influences deposition, but real plumes also experience turbulence, flocculation and resuspension. Constant settling and current velocities provide time and distance scales, not a definitive impact boundary. Release depth and bed relief must also be consistent with the coordinates used by the simplified model. Assume height above bed3m, settling speed0.02m/s and horizontal current0.30m/s. t=150s and x=45m, excluding turbulence and resuspension. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Settling and horizontal advection” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉降與水平輸運」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Settling and horizontal advection”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-37-k1","title":"沉降與水平輸運","titleEn":"Settling and horizontal advection","text":"粒子沉降與水流搬運的競爭影響落砂區，但真實濁羽還有紊流、絮凝和再懸浮。固定沉速及水平流速模型能建立時間與距離量級，不能將單一結果當成影響邊界；初始釋放深度和海床起伏也需與模型坐標一致。","textEn":"Competition between settling and advection influences deposition, but real plumes also experience turbulence, flocculation and resuspension. Constant settling and current velocities provide time and distance scales, not a definitive impact boundary.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉降與水平輸運」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Settling and horizontal advection\" is correct?","options":["粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。","粒子沉降與水流搬運的競爭影響落砂區，但真實濁羽還有紊流、絮凝和再懸浮。","施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。"],"optionsEn":["Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again.","Competition between settling and advection influences deposition, but real plumes also experience turbulence, flocculation and resuspension.","The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season."],"answer":1,"explanation":"粒子沉降與水流搬運的競爭影響落砂區，但真實濁羽還有紊流、絮凝和再懸浮。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Competition between settling and advection influences deposition, but real plumes also experience turbulence, flocculation and resuspension. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b285-v15-38","title":"沉降與水平輸運：定量估算","titleEn":"Settling and horizontal advection: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉降與水平輸運」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Settling and horizontal advection” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設距床3m、沉速0.02m/s、水平流0.30m/s，t=h/ws=150s，x=Ut=45m；忽略紊流與再懸浮。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume height above bed3m, settling speed0.02m/s and horizontal current0.30m/s. t=150s and x=45m, excluding turbulence and resuspension. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設距床3m、沉速0.02m/s、水平流0.30m/s，t=h/ws=150s，x=Ut=45m；忽略紊流與再懸浮。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume height above bed3m, settling speed0.02m/s and horizontal current0.30m/s. t=150s and x=45m, excluding turbulence and resuspension.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉降與水平輸運」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Settling and horizontal advection\", which statement holds?","options":["借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。","年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.","An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b285-v15-39","title":"沉降與水平輸運：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Settling and horizontal advection: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉降與水平輸運」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Settling and horizontal advection” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。將最簡單軌跡與實測沉積分布比較，保留偏離方向作為混合或再懸浮的證據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth. Compare the simplest trajectory with observed deposition, retaining the direction of mismatch as evidence of mixing or resuspension. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。將最簡單軌跡與實測沉積分布比較，保留偏離方向作為混合或再懸浮的證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth. Compare the simplest trajectory with observed deposition, retaining the direction of mismatch as evidence of mixing or resuspension.","failure":"注意干擾：用中值砂粒沉速代表細料會把擴散範圍算得過短，忽略潮流反轉又會放錯沉積方向。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using median-sand settling speed for fines understates plume extent, while ignoring tidal reversal misplaces deposition. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。將最簡單軌跡與實測沉積分布比較，保留偏離方向作為混合或再懸浮的證據。","textEn":"Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth. Compare the simplest trajectory with observed deposition, retaining the direction of mismatch as evidence of mixing or resuspension.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。將最簡單軌跡與實測沉積分布比較，保留偏離方向作為混合或再懸浮的證據。","textEn":"Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth. Compare the simplest trajectory with observed deposition, retaining the direction of mismatch as evidence of mixing or resuspension.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉降與水平輸運」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Settling and horizontal advection\"?","options":["以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。"],"optionsEn":["Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b285-v15-40","title":"沉降與水平輸運：失效診斷","titleEn":"Settling and horizontal advection: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉降與水平輸運」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Settling and horizontal advection” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用中值砂粒沉速代表細料會把擴散範圍算得過短，忽略潮流反轉又會放錯沉積方向。沉到床面也不保證永久固定，後續波浪可能重新輸送。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using median-sand settling speed for fines understates plume extent, while ignoring tidal reversal misplaces deposition. Reaching the bed does not establish permanent retention because later waves can mobilize and transport the same material again. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設距床3m、沉速0.02m/s、水平流0.30m/s，t=h/ws=150s，x=Ut=45m；忽略紊流與再懸浮。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume height above bed3m, settling speed0.02m/s and horizontal current0.30m/s. t=150s and x=45m, excluding turbulence and resuspension.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用中值砂粒沉速代表細料會把擴散範圍算得過短，忽略潮流反轉又會放錯沉積方向。沉到床面也不保證永久固定，後續波浪可能重新輸送。","textEn":"Using median-sand settling speed for fines understates plume extent, while ignoring tidal reversal misplaces deposition. Reaching the bed does not establish permanent retention because later waves can mobilize and transport the same material again.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉降與水平輸運」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Settling and horizontal advection\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","用中值砂粒沉速代表細料會把擴散範圍算得過短，忽略潮流反轉又會放錯沉積方向。","施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using median-sand settling speed for fines understates plume extent, while ignoring tidal reversal misplaces deposition.","The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用中值砂粒沉速代表細料會把擴散範圍算得過短，忽略潮流反轉又會放錯沉積方向。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using median-sand settling speed for fines understates plume extent, while ignoring tidal reversal misplaces deposition. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
